WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:02.890
Joe: From calorie count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:04.870
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.660
between McDonald's in Japan and the US.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.373
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.000
Hey, guys, Joe from "Food Wars."

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.500
We're doing a new season.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.545
We're comparing the US to Japan.

00:00:16.545 --> 00:00:17.940
In order to do that, I
want to introduce you

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.210
to cohost and my man in Japan, George.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.680
Hello, guys. I'm George.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.023
I'm from Japan, and I like McDonald's.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.745
So, in Japan, our McDonald's
sodas come in three sizes.

00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:36.400
This is small.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.828
Small.

00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:40.430
And this is Japan's medium.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.704
Medium.

00:00:41.704 --> 00:00:44.480
And this one is Japan's large.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.796
Large.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.611
In Japan, our chicken McNuggets

00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:53.810
come in five and 15 pieces.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.080
Our chicken McNuggets come in

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.013
four,

00:00:56.013 --> 00:00:56.990
six,

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:57.823
10,

00:00:57.823 --> 00:00:58.670
20,

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.610
or 40 piece.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.010
Look at all those nuggets.

00:01:05.072 --> 00:01:05.930
Oh.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.610
They've been sitting for a while.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.270
Japan McDonald's fries
come in three sizes,

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.610
small, medium, and large.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:14.880
In the US, you can get
your fries in four sizes,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.295
kids, small, medium, and large.

00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:22.012
Look at this little guy.
Look at this little guy.

00:01:22.012 --> 00:01:23.940
George: So, this is large fries,

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.125
and I'm going to weigh them.

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:29.310
Joe: We are going to also
weigh a large McDonald's fry.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:30.360
Wow!

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.770
OK, so, so far our larges are the same.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:33.970
Yeah, wow. That worked perfectly,

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:35.920
that thing I just did
there. Great job, Joe.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.410
Go home.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.260
Go!

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.610
Joe: Now let's measure
the medium. Why not?

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:45.356
Our mediums are smaller.

00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:47.600
Huh. Interesting.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.163
So, this is a Japanese Big Mac.

00:01:50.163 --> 00:01:51.460
Ta-da!
[trumpets playing]

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.395
Oh!

00:01:54.395 --> 00:01:56.373
So, this is a Japanese Big Mac.

00:01:56.373 --> 00:01:57.700
Joe: This is an American Big Mac,

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.492
and we're going to weigh it as well.

00:01:59.492 --> 00:02:02.330
Oh, we've got a heftier
Big Mac here in the US.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.620
That's more like it.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.490
So, in Japan, the Big Mac value set,

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:09.730
which is a Big Mac and medium
fries and a medium drink,

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:14.317
comes out to 690 yen, or $6.21.

00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:18.110
In the US, that same meal costs $8.54,

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:22.500
or 948.46 Japanese yen.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.218
That's a 37.52% increase
in price in the US.

00:02:27.218 --> 00:02:28.385
What the heck?

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.872
So, here is everything you can only get

00:02:32.872 --> 00:02:34.131
at Japan's McDonald's

00:02:34.131 --> 00:02:35.940
you cannot get in the US.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.560
And this is everything you
can get at a US McDonald's

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.090
that you cannot get in Japan.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.040
So, we are going to start
with waffle cones, right here.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.830
So, we got plain.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.960
So, plain means it's,
like, rich milk taste.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.020
And next one is strawberry.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.396
Strawberry. Personally, I like this.

00:02:54.396 --> 00:02:56.470
Our next one is

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:00.290
chocolate and almond, right there.

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.350
Mm.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:02.640
It's not melting.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.350
Good job, buddy.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.012
So, here we've got McFloats.

00:03:07.012 --> 00:03:09.230
So, McFloats means there is soda,

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.550
and on top of that, there is ice cream.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.970
That's it. That's it.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:15.518
And this is McFloats melon.

00:03:18.893 --> 00:03:20.242
Ooh!

00:03:20.242 --> 00:03:21.820
[laughs]

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.520
It's too sweet.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.786
This is grape.

00:03:24.786 --> 00:03:26.552
Coffee McFloats.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.810
Mm.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.967
And the last one,

00:03:30.967 --> 00:03:33.775
we've got Coke McFloats.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:36.960
Mm.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:41.370
Oh, Joe, you definitely try this.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.760
Yes, absolutely.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.860
I'm trying that when I go to Japan.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.850
That looks real good.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:45.830
Let me think here.

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.151
Hang on a second.

00:03:47.151 --> 00:03:48.590
[metal clanging]

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:49.423
OK.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.570
We do not have McFloats here in the US,

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.020
so I'm going to make my own.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:55.853
On the way over here,

00:03:55.853 --> 00:03:57.450
I was looking for grape soda.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.897
It's actually harder
to find than I thought.

00:03:58.897 --> 00:04:00.700
Fanta's not very popular
in the United States.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.460
But we got this.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:06.390
This is Midnight Grape
Kickstart Mountain Dew.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.503
It's grape.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.370
Haha! Left over from
the Ben &amp; Jerry's shoot.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.536
This stuff is frozen. There we go.

00:04:16.845 --> 00:04:18.770
[electric zapping]

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.540
Yeah. I'm into this.

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.530
These would do well in the US.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.760
Our cold drinks, a little bit different.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.590
We have two exclusive slushies

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.890
that you can't get in Japan.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:31.090
One is a pink lemonade.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.835
Strawberry watermelon.

00:04:32.835 --> 00:04:34.260
Yeah, dude.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.360
That looks real good.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:38.150
Yes, they do have McFlurries
and ice cream in Japan,

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.179
but one McFlurry you can
get in the US is this one.

00:04:41.179 --> 00:04:42.770
It's an M&amp;M's McFlurry.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:45.660
Sorry, it's since melted,

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.390
but it's like those mini M&amp;M's.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.358
I went to one of the few
McDonald's in the country

00:04:50.358 --> 00:04:51.923
where the ice cream machine was working.

00:04:51.923 --> 00:04:53.980
Hot caramel sundae,

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.420
and the classic

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.220
fudge sundae.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:01.550
George: So, let's go with
soft drinks, right here.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.242
Fanta grape,

00:05:03.242 --> 00:05:06.233
and here is Fanta melon.

00:05:06.233 --> 00:05:10.340
And this one is Japanese vegetable juice.

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:11.660
And there is,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.663
I guess, more than 20
or 30 vegetables in it.

00:05:14.663 --> 00:05:17.541
And it's good for health, for sure.

00:05:21.261 --> 00:05:22.401
Aah.

00:05:22.401 --> 00:05:24.716
[water running]
[chimes sound]

00:05:24.716 --> 00:05:26.420
Mm.

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:29.964
We've got Qoo white grape.

00:05:29.964 --> 00:05:31.000
Sokenbicha.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.848
Sokenbicha is like a Japanese blended tea.

00:05:33.848 --> 00:05:34.990
It's healthy.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.400
And Japanese people drink
this on a daily basis.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.241
So, next one,

00:05:39.241 --> 00:05:42.900
we've got Earl Grey iced tea.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.690
Let me show you.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.270
Wait, there is something.

00:05:48.354 --> 00:05:49.690
[beep]

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.138
There's a mosquito.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.163
I have to make a complaint,
Japan McDonald's!

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.170
Next one, we've got

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.700
oolong tea.

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.909
So, this is not actually Japanese tea.

00:06:03.909 --> 00:06:05.460
It's a Chinese tea

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.200
that's good for health as well.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.960
For health, we do have

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.964
a mango pineapple smoothie

00:06:11.964 --> 00:06:14.530
and a banana strawberry smoothie.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:16.280
Smoothies have fruit in it, right?

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.010
Oh, yeah.

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:22.363
I can just feel the nutrients
coursing through my veins!

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:28.087
So, let's start with this Hawaiian menu.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.530
This is limited.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:32.900
This one right here is Cheese Loco Moco.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.900
Ooh, it's messy.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:40.010
It's a demi-glace sauce. Man.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:41.740
And it's also got

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.057
round egg, right there,

00:06:44.057 --> 00:06:47.360
beef patty, and some cheese.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.110
I'm hungry, actually.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:52.798
Mm!

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.680
Oh, this is good!

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.663
Oh!

00:07:00.826 --> 00:07:02.167
[laughs]

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:03.540
This is [speaks Japanese],

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.010
which means really, really delicious.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:09.960
All right, so, next one,
we've got garlic shrimp,

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:13.100
and it's also got interesting bun.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.360
There is sesame on there.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.800
And deep-fried shrimp.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.651
Hawaiian barbecue potato and beef.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.650
Demi-glace sauce again.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.750
It's gonna be good.

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:30.030
This is called barbecue burger, right?

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.060
But I don't taste barbecue at all.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.070
All right, so, next one,

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:35.428
we've got Hawaiian pancake

00:07:35.428 --> 00:07:38.303
with triple berry sauce.

00:07:38.303 --> 00:07:39.816
Two pancakes.

00:07:41.228 --> 00:07:42.661
Hello!

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:45.870
Mm, smells so sweet. Ooh.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:46.978
Let's go.

00:07:50.731 --> 00:07:51.656
Ooh.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:58.554
Too sweet.

00:07:58.554 --> 00:08:01.130
McFizz blue Hawaii.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.550
Wow.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.560
It has bright blue color.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.993
This is McFizz cassis and orange.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:13.610
I would get this. I would get this.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:16.409
So, congratulations,

00:08:16.409 --> 00:08:18.313
this is the worst.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.970
OK. Breakfast time.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:24.886
This is a breakfast burrito.

00:08:24.886 --> 00:08:26.061
Ugh.

00:08:26.061 --> 00:08:30.440
Neon-yellow egg, Mexican-style salsa.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.840
Not to be confused with,
what, Canadian salsa?

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:34.820
This is actually the same burrito

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:37.415
from the US-UK thing we
shot over a year ago. So.

00:08:37.415 --> 00:08:39.800
Let's go on to these
breakfast sandwiches here.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.770
Japan does have the McGriddles,

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.160
which are a favorite of mine,

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.727
so unfortunately we will not
be talking about those today.

00:08:45.727 --> 00:08:46.870
Sad face.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:48.450
I love you, McGriddles.

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.860
So, what they don't have,

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.630
and also the UK did not have,

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.220
were our breakfast biscuit sandwiches.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.050
I don't know how to describe a biscuit,

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:59.060
other than it's dry,

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.320
it's baked.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.940
Maybe they're made with cornmeal?

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:02.820
According to the internet,

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.100
this is not a scone, so there you go.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.010
Sausage, egg, and cheese.

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:08.518
Our egg is like

00:09:08.518 --> 00:09:12.551
this fluffy, folded scrambled-egg egg.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.060
So theirs are, like, sunny-side up?

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:15.110
Ours are scrambled.

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.770
I can tell this was folded over.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:18.380
You can see the fold lines there.

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:19.960
This is how we do it in the US.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.130
Bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.190
Is there a better breakfast
combination in the world?

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:24.170
I don't think there is.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.040
Then they just have a sausage,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:26.960
no egg, no cheese,

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.940
just sausage and biscuit.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.520
We have regular-sized hotcakes,

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:33.420
and we have a hotcake-and-sausage combo.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:36.595
And, of course, comes with syrup

00:09:36.595 --> 00:09:38.901
and butter.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:43.090
Very natural pose.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.089
Very natural feeling right now.

00:09:45.089 --> 00:09:49.213
♪ Always up for a pour, yes! ♪

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.720
Breakfast is served.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:53.595
Oatmeal.

00:09:53.595 --> 00:09:55.319
On the side, to be mixed in,

00:09:55.319 --> 00:09:56.600
cranberries and raisins

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.940
and

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:58.773
diced --

00:09:58.773 --> 00:09:59.606
oh!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.646
Diced apples.

00:10:02.646 --> 00:10:03.860
[slurps]

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:07.400
And here we've got Mega Muffin.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.790
Pork patties.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.850
That's huge one.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:12.690
Mini pancakes.

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:13.973
Oh, cute.

00:10:13.973 --> 00:10:16.706
It comes with apple cream sauce.

00:10:17.969 --> 00:10:20.319
Ooh.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.440
Ooh, this is perfect for breakfast.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.760
I would get it.

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.630
Bacon egg McSandwich.

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:31.225
So, it's got bacon

00:10:31.225 --> 00:10:32.683
and round egg

00:10:32.683 --> 00:10:34.341
and cheddar cheese.

00:10:34.341 --> 00:10:35.423
That's it.

00:10:35.423 --> 00:10:37.770
And you might be surprised,

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.870
we've got Filet-O-Fish.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.995
Ta-da!

00:10:41.995 --> 00:10:44.640
So, Filet-O-Fish is on the breakfast menu.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.663
I guess Japanese people tend to

00:10:46.663 --> 00:10:48.870
eat fish for breakfast.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:50.410
Three exclusive burgers here in the US

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:53.690
are variations on the
Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.510
Yes, we've all seen "Pulp Fiction,"

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.410
we know about the whole
Quarter Pounder thing.

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:58.920
Does not exist outside of the US,

00:10:58.920 --> 00:10:59.780
I don't think.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.240
So, probably why they don't have

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.040
Quarter Pounders in Japan.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.043
The classic Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:11:05.043 --> 00:11:06.060
Look at this guy.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:09.460
I mean, this was maybe my
go-to one for a decade.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:12.220
The Quarter Pounder with cheese deluxe.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.490
I don't know.

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:15.270
I feel like this is
pretty close to a Whopper.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.520
I'm not a big Whopper guy,

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:17.720
but there you go,

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.165
a deluxe Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:11:20.165 --> 00:11:21.920
The double Quarter Pounder with cheese.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:24.020
Look at the size of this thing!

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:26.490
Yes, sir.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:29.070
Japan's exclusive burgers.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.845
Teriyaki McBurger,

00:11:30.845 --> 00:11:34.136
which is my most favorite one.

00:11:34.136 --> 00:11:37.510
My body is made of McTeriyaki burger.

00:11:39.974 --> 00:11:42.807
[angelic singing]

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:47.470
So, it's got mayo right there,

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:49.300
and lettuce, pork patties,

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.510
dip it into delicious teriyaki sauce,

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:54.740
and it's covering whole
pork patties perfectly.

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.650
Joe, when you come to
Japan, please try this.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.320
You will thank me later.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.080
Everything that they have

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:05.810
looks so good and sounds so good.

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:07.940
Man, when I go to Tokyo,

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.940
first stop, I'm going to McDonald's.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.800
Sushi, ramen, get it out of my face.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.370
I want the teriyaki burger.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.259
That's the first thing I'm
getting when I get there.

00:12:17.259 --> 00:12:18.492
Mm!

00:12:18.492 --> 00:12:20.558
I'm getting full, actually.

00:12:20.558 --> 00:12:21.523
[laughs]

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:25.271
Slow down, George. We got
a lot of food to cover.

00:12:29.137 --> 00:12:32.703
[dance music]

00:12:32.703 --> 00:12:34.520
All right, so we've got

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.320
bacon lettuce burger right here.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.810
It looks sad.

00:12:40.295 --> 00:12:42.230
Egg cheeseburger,

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:45.130
but we also call it Eguchi.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:48.600
Eguchi is an abbreviation
for egg cheeseburger.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.350
Japanese people love abbreviation.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:55.170
It's got ketchup and pickle, round egg,

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.920
and cheddar cheese and beef patties.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:58.800
Next one.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:00.930
Spicy beef burger.

00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.430
Ooh, look at this!

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:03.842
Oh, it looks so spicy!

00:13:03.842 --> 00:13:05.990
It has spicy mayo or something like that.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:10.460
So, here we've got Samurai Mac.

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.063
Samurai!

00:13:12.063 --> 00:13:13.920
Samurai Mac?

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:16.720
Yo, that sounds awesome.

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:17.970
And this blue one

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:21.885
is called roasted soy
sauce double thick beef.

00:13:21.885 --> 00:13:24.597
We've got roasted soy sauce

00:13:24.597 --> 00:13:26.650
bacon tomato thick beef.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:28.410
So if you want a little bit more, like,

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.808
healthy veggies,

00:13:30.808 --> 00:13:31.953
go for it.

00:13:31.953 --> 00:13:33.290
Uh, yeah, George, I don't know if that

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.502
makes that much healthier there

00:13:34.502 --> 00:13:37.180
'cause it also has twice
as much meat and cheese.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:39.010
If you're looking to be healthy
at a McDonald's in Japan,

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:40.700
I'd stick with the vegetable juice.

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:43.587
And this one right here is called

00:13:43.587 --> 00:13:45.597
Teriyaki chicken Filet-O.

00:13:45.597 --> 00:13:48.200
Wow. So much sauce.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:51.240
So, next one, we've got ebi Filet-O.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.300
Ebi means shrimp,

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:54.512
so it's a shrimp Filet-O.

00:13:54.512 --> 00:13:56.887
Oh, yeah. It's got aurora sauce.

00:13:56.887 --> 00:14:00.820
Aurora sauce is like
ketchup and mayonnaise.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.770
So, it's got a lot of shrimp in there.

00:14:05.112 --> 00:14:06.312
Mm!

00:14:06.312 --> 00:14:08.412
So good. So good.

00:14:08.412 --> 00:14:09.650
In the US, we have about

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:13.480
four exclusive chicken
sandwiches specifically.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:14.650
I didn't see this on the menu,

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.530
but apparently you guys
don't have a McChicken,

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:20.852
which is just chicken sandwich.

00:14:20.852 --> 00:14:23.460
Regular bun, mayo,

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.293
chicken.

00:14:25.435 --> 00:14:26.410
Yeah.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:27.670
We also have,

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.407
check this out, spicy McChicken.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.270
So pretty much the same McChicken,

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:33.497
but they put spicy coating

00:14:33.497 --> 00:14:35.550
on the breading on the chicken.

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:38.450
Every fast-food chain in America right now

00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:39.315
is having what we're calling

00:14:39.315 --> 00:14:41.070
the fried-chicken-sandwich wars.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:44.530
Popeyes, Burger King,
of course McDonald's,

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.662
all of them are at this arms race

00:14:46.662 --> 00:14:47.930
to have the best chicken sandwich.

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.970
I think 'cause Chick-fil-A
has edged everyone out.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:53.200
These are the three that
are currently available.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.840
I don't know for how long.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.265
You have the crispy chicken sandwich.

00:14:56.265 --> 00:14:58.490
I think it's a brioche bun,

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:01.850
pickles, and no sauce,
which I think is strange.

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:03.020
So, like, the whole flavor

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.753
is just the chicken.

00:15:04.753 --> 00:15:07.640
Spicy chicken sandwich.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:08.740
Same deal,

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:13.026
but, of course, spicy sauce.

00:15:13.026 --> 00:15:16.180
And the spicy chicken deluxe,

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.870
which, to George's point,

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:19.303
has more vegetables on it.

00:15:19.303 --> 00:15:22.120
You know, to be healthier.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.510
OK, so when it comes to side menus,

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:28.250
we've got Shaka Shaka Chicken,

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.616
and we have

00:15:29.616 --> 00:15:30.750
two fla --
[thunder rumbles]

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:31.583
oh!

00:15:31.583 --> 00:15:32.960
Two flavors.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:36.574
Can you hear that?
Thunder, thunder, thunder!

00:15:36.574 --> 00:15:38.900
'Cause it's rainy season in Japan.

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:41.870
It's the sunny season here
in Southern California.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:44.473
And here is red pepper.

00:15:44.473 --> 00:15:46.691
And this one is cheddar cheese.

00:15:46.691 --> 00:15:49.866
[thundering]

00:15:49.866 --> 00:15:51.700
Thunder, stop!

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.010
So, all you have to do is just

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.195
put the powder into the bag

00:15:55.195 --> 00:15:57.019
and shake it.

00:15:57.019 --> 00:15:59.769
[paper rattling]

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.848
And the powder should be covering

00:16:03.848 --> 00:16:05.835
the whole Shaka Chicken.
[thundering]

00:16:05.835 --> 00:16:07.940
Ooh, big one!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.248
Like this.

00:16:13.753 --> 00:16:16.130
This I've seen before. This I want.

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:18.320
That's the thing I want the
most at a Japanese McDonald's.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.560
US McDonald's, we have the bags,

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:22.160
we have the chicken.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:25.350
Just get the spice packets. Throw it in.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:28.010
George: We've got side salad,

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:32.130
and it comes with this
roasted sesame dressing.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.460
Let's go!

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:35.940
Ooh.

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:37.150
That was cool.

00:16:37.150 --> 00:16:38.572
Now put it all in the garbage.

00:16:38.572 --> 00:16:41.481
We've got edamame and corn.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:43.767
Yogurt,

00:16:43.767 --> 00:16:46.370
and there's cow,

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.470
cow.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:48.870
Exclusive sauces.

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.480
It's sauce talk time.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.012
Sauce Talk.

00:16:52.012 --> 00:16:54.610
We have sweet 'n sour sauce.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.120
They gave me

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.730
hot mustard.

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:59.420
This was supposed to be honey mustard.

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:00.600
You guys have hot mustard?

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.010
I know you don't have honey mustard.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.753
Of course, ranch.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:08.010
Ooh, spicy Buffalo.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.112
Now, these might be promotions

00:17:09.112 --> 00:17:12.810
'cause of that singing group BTS,

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.940
but we have right now a

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.660
Cajun sauce and a sweet chili sauce.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:21.117
This sauce is fantastic.

00:17:21.117 --> 00:17:23.190
This is the sauce. This
has to stay on the menu.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.680
So, these two are new ones.

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:28.210
This one right here is

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.291
soy sauce, best sauce.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.240
Man. This is fantastic!

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.250
Good job!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.170
Very good taste.

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.670
So, this one right here is called

00:17:40.670 --> 00:17:42.310
Louisiana hot sauce.

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:45.893
Ooh, it does look like very spicy one.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.760
This is not spicy at all.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:55.590
Actually, we were supposed
to have bai burger options,

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.800
but unfortunately you can
only get them from 5:30 p.m.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:01.230
But let me explain what bai burger is.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:04.210
Bai simply means double in Japanese.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:06.240
So if you order a normal Big Mac,

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:08.040
it has two beef patties, right?

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:10.340
But if you order bai Big Mac,

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:11.840
it has four beef patties.

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:14.760
But not only Big Mac, but all burgers

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:17.030
adopts the bai burger options.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:17.863
That's funny.

00:18:17.863 --> 00:18:19.800
You can only get double
the meat after 5:30,

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:20.770
that's really funny.

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:23.520
That would not stand
in this country at all.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:25.690
People would lose their minds.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:27.870
Four patties?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.430
On a Big Mac?

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:30.770
So after shooting this video,

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:33.120
I'm going to order bai Big Mac.

00:18:33.120 --> 00:18:35.700
And then bye-bye, health.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:37.450
You ain't gotta tell me, George!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:38.608
Bye, health!

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:42.900
All right, here are all the ingredients

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:44.545
for a US Big Mac.

00:18:44.545 --> 00:18:45.378
Oh, God.

00:18:45.378 --> 00:18:46.608
The bun. It has:

00:18:46.608 --> 00:18:48.116
enriched flour, which is wheat flour,

00:18:48.116 --> 00:18:50.580
[fast-forwarding]

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.930
vinegar, and contains wheat.

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:54.010
On to the beef patty.

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:57.110
100% pure USDA inspected beef,

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.010
no fillers, no extenders!

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:00.600
Prepared on the grill with seasoning,

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:01.960
salt and black pepper.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:03.670
There you go. There you go.

00:19:03.670 --> 00:19:05.110
Try the lettuce ingredients,

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.170
lettuce.

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:07.170
Nice.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.930
The Big Mac sauce ingredients.

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.331
Soybean oil,

00:19:10.331 --> 00:19:13.079
[fast-forwarding]

00:19:13.079 --> 00:19:16.592
extractives of paprika, soy lecithin.

00:19:16.592 --> 00:19:17.470
[burps]

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:19.100
The pickle slice ingredients.

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.970
Cucumbers, water, distilled vinegar,

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.610
salt, calcium chloride, alum,

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.650
potassium sorbate as a preservative,

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.630
natural flavors, polysorbate 80,

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.780
extractives of turmeric for color.

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:30.880
Onion ingredients.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:31.713
Onions.

00:19:31.713 --> 00:19:32.762
There you go.

00:19:32.762 --> 00:19:34.310
A few things I want to note.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.140
Alum is used to dissolve steel.

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:41.240
Polysorbate 80 has been linked
to colon cancer in mice.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.602
Cue the dancing mice.

00:19:42.602 --> 00:19:46.360
[dance music]

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:49.240
And caramel color is on
California's list of chemicals

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:52.460
that may cause cancer and
reproductive toxicity,

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:53.630
good God.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:54.650
Counterpoint.

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:56.340
They all taste fantastic.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.630
So, McDonald's Japan doesn't disclose

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.680
their ingredients in the Big Mac.

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:04.970
However, they do tell us where
the ingredients come from.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.890
If you order a Big Mac in Japan,

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:10.750
you'll eat beef from
Australia or New Zealand;

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.260
buns made from wheat
imported from the USA,

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:16.450
Canada, and Australia;

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:19.880
and pickles made from
cucumbers grown in Turkey,

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:22.090
Sri Lanka, or India;

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:25.660
onions grown in the USA or India;

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:28.260
sliced cheddar cheese made in New Zealand,

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:31.570
Australia, the USA, or Japan;

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.660
and lettuce grown in Japan,

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:37.350
Taiwan, the USA, or Malaysia.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:40.380
The only ingredients that come from Japan

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:42.690
are the cheese and the lettuce.

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:45.880
And even then, McDonald's
still imports some lettuce

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:48.120
and cheese from other countries.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:51.053
So this is a very international burger.

00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:53.258
Thank you, world!

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:59.975
In Japan, our Big Mac is 525 calories

00:20:59.975 --> 00:21:02.555
and 28.3 grams of fat

00:21:02.555 --> 00:21:06.067
and 1,007 milligrams of sodium

00:21:06.067 --> 00:21:09.220
and 41.8 grams of carbs

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.820
and 26 grams of protein.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:15.250
In the US, our Big Mac is 550 calories,

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.291
30 grams of fat,

00:21:16.291 --> 00:21:18.540
1,010 milligrams of sodium,

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.865
45 grams of carbs,

00:21:19.865 --> 00:21:22.431
and 25 grams of protein.

00:21:22.431 --> 00:21:23.970
So the US has a slight increase

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.230
on everything except protein.

00:21:26.230 --> 00:21:28.612
So, in Japan, our five-piece nuggets

00:21:28.612 --> 00:21:30.760
is 270 calories

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.440
and 17.2 grams of fat

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:36.330
and 506 milligrams of sodium

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:39.250
and 13.1 grams of carbs

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:42.290
and 15.8 grams of protein.

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:45.300
Broken down, each nugget is 54 calories.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.810
We don't have a five-piece here in the US,

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:48.210
but we do have this, a 10-piece.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:49.850
Let's get those stats on the screen.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:51.400
Go ahead and divide everything by two,

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:54.240
and, yes, now we have the
stats for a five-piece.

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:55.270
Pretty smart, eh?

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:57.820
If we want to divide all
that by, I think, five,

00:21:57.820 --> 00:22:00.504
you'll get the stats for one nugget.

00:22:00.504 --> 00:22:02.720
[sighs] This is so exhausting.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:04.860
In Japan, if you order a Big Mac meal

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:08.310
with large fries and a
medium chocolate shake,

00:22:08.310 --> 00:22:12.007
the grand total will be 1,405 calories.

00:22:12.007 --> 00:22:14.010
And in the US, adding medium fries

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:15.970
and a medium chocolate shake to a Big Mac,

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:19.360
the grand total is 1,660 calories.

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:23.870
And that is a calorie increase of 18.14%.

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.640
If you're wondering why
we're using a large fry

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:27.210
but a medium chocolate shake,

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:28.590
it turns out that in Japan,

00:22:28.590 --> 00:22:31.165
you can't get a large chocolate shake.

00:22:31.165 --> 00:22:32.850
They'll only sell it to you in medium.

00:22:32.850 --> 00:22:33.900
I'm assuming because they don't want you

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:36.200
eating that much ice cream.

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.070
Hey, thanks for watching.

00:22:37.070 --> 00:22:39.900
If you enjoyed this US versus
Japan McDonald's episode,

00:22:39.900 --> 00:22:43.323
check out our US versus UK
McDonald's episode right here.

